--- Message Type Help ---
{
  "envelope": {
    "subject": {
      "use": "notUsed",
      "forms": [],
      "description": "No subject is used; the template and the batch are sent in data."
    },
    "dataRequired": true,
    "version": "1.0",
    "contentType": "text/json"
  },
  "target": [
    {
      "source": "data.journalTemplateName, data.journalBatchName",
      "form": "journal template and batch name",
      "description": "The item journal template and batch that hold the reclassification lines."
    }
  ],
  "parameters": [
    {
      "name": "journalTemplateName",
      "type": "string",
      "required": true,
      "description": "Item journal template name, at most 10 characters; read as an upper-case code. Use a reclassification template (type Transfer); other template types are refused before posting."
    },
    {
      "name": "journalBatchName",
      "type": "string",
      "required": true,
      "description": "Name of the journal batch to post, at most 10 characters; read as an upper-case code. Every line of the batch is posted."
    }
  ],
  "response": {
    "contentType": "text/json",
    "fields": [
      {
        "name": "status",
        "type": "string",
        "description": "Success when the batch was posted."
      },
      {
        "name": "journalTemplateName",
        "type": "string",
        "description": "The template that was posted, as read from the request."
      },
      {
        "name": "journalBatchName",
        "type": "string",
        "description": "The batch that was posted, as read from the request."
      }
    ]
  },
  "errors": [
    {
      "code": "RecordNotFound",
      "when": "The journal template does not exist.",
      "fix": "Send the name of an existing Transfer journal template."
    },
    {
      "code": "PreconditionFailed",
      "when": "The journal template is not of type Transfer.",
      "fix": "Use a reclassification template; use the dedicated posting message for other journal types."
    },
    {
      "code": "MissingParameter",
      "when": "journalTemplateName is absent.",
      "fix": "Send journalTemplateName."
    },
    {
      "code": "MissingParameter",
      "when": "journalBatchName is absent.",
      "fix": "Send journalBatchName."
    },
    {
      "code": "InvalidParameter",
      "when": "The Reclassification domain is turned off for this company in Inventory Setup.",
      "fix": "Turn the domain on from the Inventory Setup page."
    },
    {
      "code": "PermissionDenied",
      "when": "The caller lacks the posting permission set Inv. Posting Gate.",
      "fix": "Ask an administrator for Inv. Posting Gate."
    },
    {
      "code": "BusinessCentralError",
      "error": "Reclassification batch %1 %2 has no lines.",
      "when": "The batch has no lines or does not exist. The answer carries the error text and no code.",
      "fix": "Check journalTemplateName and journalBatchName, or create the lines first."
    },
    {
      "code": "BusinessCentralError",
      "error": "Business Central posting error text",
      "when": "The batch posting fails, for example because a line fails the item journal checks. The posting is rolled back and the answer carries the error text and no code.",
      "fix": "Correct the line named in the text and retry."
    }
  ],
  "effect": {
    "effect": "irreversible",
    "changes": "Posts every line of the item journal batch through the standard item journal batch posting: item ledger and value entries are created, an item register is written and the posted lines leave the journal. The posting commits. It does not create or post a transfer order.",
    "idempotent": false,
    "permissionSet": "Bifrost Full Access and Inv. Posting Gate",
    "writes": true,
    "posts": true
  },
  "metering": {
    "chargeable": true,
    "chargedAs": "message"
  },
  "related": [
    {
      "name": "Inventory.Reclassification.Check",
      "useInsteadWhen": "Use it first to confirm that the template is a reclassification template."
    },
    {
      "name": "Inventory.Reclassification.PreviewPost",
      "useInsteadWhen": "Use it first to list the lines that the posting would process."
    }
  ],
  "workflow": {
    "steps": [
      {
        "messageType": "Inventory.Reclassification.Check",
        "purpose": "Confirm that the template is a reclassification template and see how many transfer lines the batch has."
      },
      {
        "messageType": "Inventory.Reclassification.PreviewPost",
        "purpose": "Simulate native posting and inspect the rolled-back ledger entries."
      },
      {
        "messageType": "Inventory.Reclassification.Post",
        "purpose": "Post the batch; the lines are written to the item ledger."
      }
    ]
  },
  "examples": [
    {
      "title": "Post the reclassification batch DEFAULT",
      "request": {
        "type": "Inventory.Reclassification.Post",
        "data": {
          "journalTemplateName": "RECLASS",
          "journalBatchName": "DEFAULT"
        }
      },
      "response": {
        "status": "Success",
        "journalTemplateName": "RECLASS",
        "journalBatchName": "DEFAULT"
      }
    }
  ],
  "overview": "Posts every line of a reclassification journal batch through the standard item journal batch posting. Posting is permanent and needs the Inv. Posting Gate permission set.",
  "notes": "Posting is permanent and commits. All lines of the batch are posted; the call has no line selection. It does not create or post a transfer order. The call requires an existing reclassification (Transfer) template before it reads or posts any journal line. Missing templates return RecordNotFound; other template types return PreconditionFailed with a nextStep. A batch without lines, or one that does not exist, is answered with the error text and no code. A posting error is answered with Business Central's text and no code, and the posting is rolled back. The caller needs the Inv. Posting Gate permission set (without it the call is not listed as enabled) and the table permissions that the standard item journal posting itself needs. The Reclassification domain must be turned on in Inventory Setup (a missing setup row counts as on). Use Inventory.Reclassification.Check first. Inventory.Reclassification.PreviewPost runs native posting preview, returns captured ledger entries and rolls back the simulated posting changes."
}

## Errors and warnings
An error response has `status` = `Error`, a stable `code`, the `error` text and, when they apply, `parameter` (the request parameter concerned, e.g. `lines[2].no`), `received` (the value received), `expected` (what was expected) and `nextStep` (what to do now). `hint` says where to read more.
When a request has several problems, all of them are listed in `errors[]` - each with the same fields - under a top-level `code` (`MultipleErrors`, or a shared code such as `InvalidLine` for the `lines` of a Create type) and a summary `error`. Fix them all before calling again. One problem is reported at the top level, with no `errors[]`.
Request values are checked first and every problem found is reported together. A Business Central validation error raised afterwards, while a record is being written, stops the call and is reported on its own: `code` = `BusinessCentralError`, Business Central's own `error` text, and `parameter` naming the request parameter being applied, e.g. `lines[1].accountNo`. Nothing is written.
Request values are read in one format, whatever the language: dates `YYYY-MM-DD`; date-times ISO 8601 with `Z` or an offset; amounts as JSON numbers (or a string such as `"1234.56"`, no thousands separator); integers as JSON integers; booleans `true` or `false`. Any other value is `InvalidParameterFormat` with `received` and `expected`; for an unambiguous local form such as `26.09.2026`, `nextStep` gives the value to resend. Every bad value of a request is reported together.
Answers are written in one format as well, whatever the language of the call: dates `YYYY-MM-DD`, date-times ISO 8601, numbers with a dot and no thousands separator, and the option and enum values of every answer except `Data.Records.Get` and `Data.Records.Set` as their English names, so a value read from an answer can be sent back. Those two answer the caption of the language of the call, for a person to read. The language of the call (`lcid`) changes captions and message texts, not these forms. Two things are outside Bifrost's control: Business Central writes its own texts (a ledger entry description such as `Direct Cost V00010 on 10/02/26`, the text of a `BusinessCentralError`) with the regional settings of the server session, which `lcid` does not change, so a date in such a text can be in month-day order; and a table view is read with those settings too, so write dates in a view as `YYYY-MM-DD` and decimals with a dot.
Both success and error responses can carry `warnings[]`, each with `code`, `message` and, when they apply, `parameter` and `nextStep`.
`UnknownParameter` refuses undeclared data keys before execution for every type whose effect is not read, including a missing effect. The root envelope option `strict:false` cannot opt out. Read types keep warnings without changing status, validationResult or domain warningCount unless the caller sets `strict:true` (next to type and subject, never inside data). Refusals list the keys and localized nextStep corrections; no business changes or successful execution charges occur. Example: {"type":"Memory.User.Set","strict":true,"data":{"memory":"test","memry":"typo"}} is refused.
`FieldChangedByBC` is a warning from Data.Records.Set: another field validation or the write changed a sent field after its own validation. `parameter` names data[n].fields.{jsonName}, counting from 0. Status stays Success. Compare the returned values with what you sent; follow `nextStep` to use validation order or send the field again in a separate call. Normalisation of the field itself, LCY, Dimension Set ID, BLOB, Media, MediaSet and skipped fields are excluded.
Feature apps (Foundation 28.0.8 or later) can call `Argument.SetErrorContext(Parameter, Expected, NextStep)` before an operation that may fail after writes, then `Argument.ClearErrorContext()` after success. Supply the parameter name and translated labels, never request values, file content, credentials or a call stack. Foundation returns that context on the original `BusinessCentralError` after rollback, including uncaught task errors; `RespondWithLastError()` also uses it. The API does not catch errors, commit data or change the transaction boundary. Keep no-return `Codeunit.Run` and let errors propagate for chained `OmitCommit` calls; never add a Boolean `Codeunit.Run` or a writing `TryFunction` to recover context. Context is cleared between messages. Existing callers without context keep their response shape; recognized lock errors keep their existing `Retryable` guidance.
A message type that must run only one way (Foundation 28.0.9 or later) reads `Argument.GetInvocationSource()`: `Queue` when the task scheduler runs a message the queue API scheduled, `Task` for the Task API (`/tasks`), `Dispatcher` for an internal call through `Dispatcher ori` (the in-product MCP tool server, a nested dispatch from another message type), `Direct` for the Messages page Run Task action and anything unset. Only Foundation sets it; request values, parameters, source, subject and writes to the argument cannot change it. Refuse the other paths with `PreconditionFailed` and a `nextStep` that names the path to use.
`Retryable` means a transient lock or deadlock caught while writing or posting. `error` keeps Business Central's original text. `expected` is "no concurrent lock on the same records"; `nextStep` is "Retry the same call after a few seconds; nothing was changed." Bifrost does not retry automatically. Other platform errors, including uncaught queue-path errors, remain `BusinessCentralError`.
Codes: `MissingParameter`, `InvalidParameterFormat`, `InvalidParameter`, `RecordNotFound`, `AmbiguousRecord`, `ConflictingIdentifiers`, `InvalidFilterField`, `InvalidLine`, `NothingToPreview`, `LinesSkipped`, `BlockedByWriteGuard`, `PreconditionFailed`, `PermissionDenied`, `LimitExceeded`, `BusinessCentralError`, `MultipleErrors`, `DeprecatedParameter`, `UnknownParameter`, `FieldChangedByBC`, `Retryable`, `EULA_REQUIRED`, `TRIAL_NOT_STARTED`. The `error` text may be translated; the code never is.
